

        From    Mark Durbin. (Unisys Ltd.)
        To      John Evans   (I.T.)
        Date    4th June 1991
        Subject Critical Error Handlers.



    John,

        I thought I would clear up a few points about critical 
        error handlers.


        There are four possible return values from a critical error 
        handler :

        Abort   -       Return to the operating system

        Retry   -       Try again from the same position

        Ignore  -       Ignore this error and try the next operation

        Fail    -       Return an error to the calling application

        The standard PC-MOS/DOS printer critical error handlers will
        give the options to Abort Retry or Ignore.  This error is 
        generated and operated upon by the operating system NOT the 
        printer driver.
        
        This is why there is an installable handler within the VM 
        sub-system.  Once the handler is installed it will always
        return Fail,  thereby letting the application cope with
        the error in a context sensitive way.  This error handler
        can be modified to offer any or all of the above four
        options.

        Please don't hesitate to contact me if this is not clear.

            Regards,

                Mark.
